## Original Content
Производство первичного алюминия в странах Персидского залива в июле составило 293 тыс. тонн, что на 44% меньше объема за тот же месяц 2025 года, согласно предварительным расчетам Международного института алюминия (IAI).

## Summary
Production of primary aluminum in the Persian Gulf countries dropped by 44% year-over-year in July to 293,000 tons, according to preliminary calculations by the International Aluminum Institute (IAI). This significant decline highlights a substantial reduction in aluminum output in the region. The decrease may reflect various factors such as reduced demand, production constraints, or economic shifts.

## Key Points
- 44% year-over-year decrease in primary aluminum production in the Persian Gulf in July
- July production volume: 293,000 tons
- Source: Preliminary calculations by the International Aluminum Institute (IAI)


